WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:06.640
Now let's talk about the suite of technologies&nbsp;
that make civilization 3.0 possible

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:13.840
The first&nbsp;is what I call mobile real&nbsp;
estate. We're also advancing in the area&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:20.640
of what google's Astro Teller calls mobile&nbsp;
infrastructure -- even movable cities.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:27.040
First, they're settled communities with&nbsp;
a very light footprint; we're investing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:32.400
in the technologies to nourish ourselves&nbsp;
without destabilizing the environment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:39.200
The Dutch for example have a national circular&nbsp;
strategy and towns that collect rain water and do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:45.200
wastewater treatment and recycling they have solar&nbsp;
power and hydro and aquaponic agriculture. Okay,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:49.440
small and mobile villages: that&nbsp;
sounds good for millions of people.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:56.320
What about for hundreds of millions of&nbsp;
people? What about places like cairo? Cairo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:02.880
faces insufficient Nile river water, while&nbsp;
Alexandria faces a rising Mediterranean sea.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:09.280
The people of Alexandria and Cairo need&nbsp;
desalination and they need more efficient&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:17.920
crop irrigation, but beware of spending billions&nbsp;
of dollars on irrigation to sustain agriculture&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:23.920
in places where the water supply is at risk&nbsp;
and the delicate range of air temperature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:30.080
that's right for growing food. Ultimately,&nbsp;
many people in egypt will have to relocate.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:38.560
Skyscrapers could well become the stranded&nbsp;
assets and detritus of our present civilization&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:46.640
like the pyramids of ancient Egypt or&nbsp;
they may become air-conditioned shelters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:54.160
part of an archipelago of mixed-use facilities&nbsp;
all within a domed city; which is exactly what's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.160 --> 00:02:01.920
being planned for parts of Dubai. If we stay&nbsp;
where we are we are at best a survival society;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:07.840
instead, we should move and we should build anew.

